<</Producer(ABBYY FineReader 12 Sprint)/CreationDate(D:20230817031734Z)/ModDate(D:20230816194548-05'00')/Author(Warren Treadgold)/Creator()/Title(Byzantine Historiography and the Supposedly Lost Books of Ammianus Marcellinus \(book chapter\))/Subject(Parts of a missing work are located in the works of other historians who used Ammianus)/Keywords(History, Historical, Historiography, Roman, Roman Empire, Byzantine, Byzantium, Byzantine Empire, Asia Minor, Chronicles, Ammianus, Eustathius, John of Antioch, Zonaras, Scutariotes, Writing, Literature\r\n\r\nByzantine Historiography and the Supposedly Lost Books of Ammianus Marcellinus, by Warren Treadgold, from Texts and Studies in Eastern Christianity, volume 16, Armenia between Byzantium and the Orient, Celebrating the Memory of Karen Yuzbashyan \(1927- 2009\), multiple editors \(Boston, 2020\), pp. 530-579, in 50 bookmarked and searchable pdf pages. The first 13 books of the Roman History of author Ammianus Marcellinus are missing...or are they? Wikipedia has a group of entries about the 4th-century historian Ammianus. Internet Archive has other works by the distinguished philologist.)>>
endobj
